  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Which of the following statements are true in relation to the function $f(x)=(0.125)^{x}?$\n\n- Its domain is $x>0$\n- Its range is $-\\infty <y<\\infty $\n- It has a horizontal asymptote $y=0$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's start by recalling the graph of $y=(0.125)^{x}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13941630/assets/20fae3a813e249a6423567b448a1f5515c3b9127e7c0b82aad541e720db03aca.png)\n\nLet's go through the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function $f(x)=(0.125)^{x}$ is defined for all input values $x,$ so the domain is $-\\infty <x<\\infty .$\n\n- Statement II is false. The set of possible outputs of $f(x)=(0.125)^{x}$ consists of all the positive numbers, so the range is $y>0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. As $x$ increases, the function value gets smaller and smaller, approaching zero. Therefore $y=0$ is a horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x).$\n\nIn conclusion, only statement III is true.",
